		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Problème avec la fonction now()]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=35107#p35107"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Version courte poour reproduire :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>select &#039;Before begin&#039;, now();
begin;
select &#039;In begin - 1&#039;, now();</code></pre></div><p>Attendre un peu</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>select &#039;In begin - 2&#039;, now();
end;
select &#039;After begin&#039;, now();</code></pre></div><p>Result :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>   ?column?   |              now
--------------+-------------------------------
 Before begin | 2024-06-10 11:01:59.470195+02
(1 row)

BEGIN

   ?column?   |              now
--------------+-------------------------------
 In begin - 1 | 2024-06-10 11:01:59.470478+02
(1 row)

   ?column?   |              now
--------------+-------------------------------
 In begin - 2 | 2024-06-10 11:01:59.470478+02
(1 row)

COMMIT

  ?column?   |              now
-------------+-------------------------------
 After begin | 2024-06-10 11:02:10.642165+02
(1 row)</code></pre></div><p>==&gt; &quot;Begin&quot; &quot;fige&quot; la fonction now(); Comment faire pour avoir le véritable timestamp ?</p>]]></content>
